# Secrets-scan allowlist — see .github/scripts/check-secrets.py
#
# For documented false positives only: a `password = "..."` in an example
# config, a test fixture carrying a synthetic token. A real credential is never
# allowlisted — it is rotated, then removed from history.
#
# Entry form:
#   <path>:<lineno>
#
# Stale entries (file gone, or a non-numeric line) are reported as warnings on
# every run so this file does not quietly rot.
